{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Builds a traceable Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog from the saved design document or, if absent, the saved requirements summary, then generates the supplied workbook with editable USD assumptions.",
        "tags": ["safe-backlog", "wsjf", "process-engineering"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Create an Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog from the saved requirements.",
            "Generate an Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog from the design, including epics, features, and stories.",
            "Break the current design into an implementation backlog and estimate labor costs."
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Portfolio_Backlog_Pipeline",
            "function": {
                "description": "Reads the saved design document, or the saved requirements summary if no design exists, and creates a traceable Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog workbook with WSJF formulas and editable USD cost assumptions.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's request, passed through for context."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
# ROLE
Generate one traceable Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog from one saved source artifact, and save it with
the supplied Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog workbook template. Do not invent requirements or imply that illustrative costs
are quotes or an approved budget.

# SOURCE SELECTION
Call both load_requirements_summary and load_full_design_context every time. Stop and report
explicitly if either returns status ERROR. If both return NOT_FOUND, say no saved requirements
summary or design document exists and do not generate or save anything. If a design exists, use it
as the sole source; it takes precedence over a requirements summary and must not be merged with it.
Otherwise use the requirements summary. Do not substitute cloud architecture or inline text for
the required saved source.

For design, inspect the returned master_process, including requirements, high_level_design.components,
low_level_design.components, interfaces, constraints, and operating/deployment details when present.
For requirements, inspect requirements_register and its scope, stakeholders, dependencies, risks,
assumptions, and open questions. Preserve exact source requirement IDs and design component names in
traces_to. Do not assume missing fields exist.

# BACKLOG
Save one JSON object with name, summary, source_artifact (exactly "design" or
"requirements_summary"), source_name, and a non-empty epics array. Nest non-empty features under
epics and non-empty stories under features. Give every item a unique id with EPIC-001, FEAT-001,
or STORY-001 prefixes, plus title, description, strategic_theme, non-empty traces_to, priority_components,
and job_size. Every story also needs a non-empty acceptance_criteria array of observable pass/fail
outcomes.

priority_components must contain integer user_business_value, time_criticality, and risk_reduction
scores. Each component and job_size must use only the modified Fibonacci values [1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13,
20]. State defaults to In Analysis unless the selected source explicitly gives a lifecycle state.
Scores are relative planning judgments, never currency. Cover material security, privacy, access
control, integration, resilience, migration, and operational work when present in the source.
Create enabler work only when needed to deliver source-backed scope. Do not invent commitments,
dates, team capacity, project-specific rates, licenses, or cloud costs.

Before saving, verify unique IDs, valid score scales, traceability for every item, testable story
acceptance criteria, and that each epic has a feature and each feature has a story.

# SAVE AND RESPONSE
Call save_portfolio_backlog with the complete backlog JSON. If the result starts with ERROR, report
the error and do not claim success. Otherwise report the chosen source, epic/feature/story counts,
and the exact JSON/workbook paths returned. Costs are illustrative USD delivery-labor planning
estimates; the workbook's Assumptions worksheet retains the estimate method, effort-per-point, and
contingency assumptions, while the separate Role Rates worksheet lists the TBD people, role mix, and
illustrative daily rates. Each backlog line item identifies its costed role mix or indicates that it
rolls up child-item costs. Clearly call out that names/rates and estimates must be validated before
funding decisions. They are not quotes or an approved budget.
""",
            "tools": [
                "load_requirements_summary",
                "design_json_tool",
                "save_portfolio_backlog"
            ]
        },

        {
            "name": "load_requirements_summary",
            "function": {
                "description": "Loads the saved requirements summary, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."
            },
            "class": "load_requirements_summary_tool.LoadRequirementsSummaryCodedTool"
        },

        {
            "name": "design_json_tool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Loads the saved design document's full context, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."
            },
            "class": "design_json_tool.LoadFullDesignContextCodedTool"
        },

        {
            "name": "save_portfolio_backlog",
            "function": {
                "description": "Persists the generated Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog JSON and workbook.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "backlog": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "description": "The complete Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog with nested epics, features, stories, source traceability, priority scores, and acceptance criteria."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["backlog"]
                }
            },
            "class": "save_portfolio_backlog_tool.SavePortfolioBacklogCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
